[b]◈ THE OLIVE YARD[/b]
*line_break
Beside the flat yard of beaten earth, a wooden beam scale hangs from a sturdy frame near stacked wicker baskets and waiting carts. A thickset man in his late forties stands beside the pans in a dark wool coat that smells of wine and crushed fruit, grey stubble shadowing a heavy jaw and a heavy club resting at his belt. Two broad men in dusty work shirts lean against the nearest cart.

In front of the scale stands a young woman in her early twenties with dark braided hair and dust along the hem of her skirt. A basket heaped to the rim with dark olives sits on one iron pan. The man in the dark coat drops a heavy brass weight onto the other pan; the beam tips sharply, and the basket rises.

"Twelve pounds short," the bailiff says flatly, writing a mark on a scrap of paper. "Same as last month. Your mother's lease sits two seasons in arrears now, girl."

"That basket is packed to the brim," the young woman says, her voice tight. "Two people carried it down off the terrace."

The bailiff catches her by the wrist, pulling her a step closer to the scale. "House Ferrand's brass does not lie. Come up to the pressing house at dusk, and we will settle your mother's balance off the books."

*set met_house_ferrand true
*choice
  # Step in and tell him to let go of her wrist.@{show_stat_hints  [Persuasion or Intimidation DC 13]|}
    *goto pc_sw_day_intervene
  # Watch the brass weight on the scale pan closely.@{show_stat_hints  [Perception or Investigation DC 12]|}
    *goto pc_sw_day_watch
  # Leave them to it and return to the lane.
    You step back past the stacked baskets without drawing the bailiff's eye. A moment later the young woman pulls her wrist free, shoulders rigid, and heads down the lane with her empty basket.
    *page_break Back to Palmcote's lane…
    *goto pc_sw_exit_lane

*label pc_sw_day_intervene
*set scenery_subplace "palmcote_olive_yard"
You step onto the edge of the yard, meeting the bailiff's gaze levelly.  "Take your hand off her."
*gosub_scene dice_engine roll_skill_check 13 "persuasion" "" "intimidation" "" "" ""
*if (check_success)
  *set pc_sw_stood_up_day true
  The bailiff measures your posture for two slow seconds, glances toward the watching pickers by the carts, and drops her wrist with a sour grunt.

  "Mind your own road, stranger," he says coldly. "House Ferrand's business is no concern of drifters."

  The young woman rubs her bruised wrist, gives you one sharp, grateful look under her brows, and hurries back toward the lower cottages before he can speak again.
*else
  *set pc_sw_kelm_wary true
  The bailiff's mouth twists into an ugly smirk. Behind him, both men by the cart straighten up and lift stout wooden cart stakes from the dirt.

  "Please, leave it," the young woman whispers quickly, pulling her wrist free herself and stepping back from you. "He will take it out on my mother if you fight here."

  "Listen to the girl," the bailiff tells you, studying your face so he will know it again. "Move along."
*page_break Return to Palmcote's lane…
*goto pc_sw_exit_lane

