Near the roofed stone well at the bend in the lane, a hound bays sharply up on the dark terraces. Loose stones clatter down a drystone wall.
*gosub pc_sw_outdoor_sky

A young woman vaults the low terrace wall right beside the well, landing hard on one knee in the dirt.
*if (pc_sw_saw_yard)
  It is the olive picker from the yard. Blood beads at the corner of her split lip, and she hugs a heavy oilcloth bundle tightly against her ribs.
*else
  She is in her early twenties, dark braid coming loose over one shoulder, blood beading at the corner of a fresh split lip, hugging a heavy oilcloth bundle tightly against her ribs.

Thirty paces up the slope, two shuttered lanterns swing wildly between the twisted olive trunks as two armed men crash down the terrace steps behind a thick-necked estate hound straining at its leash.

The woman grabs your sleeve, chest heaving. "Don't shout, please," she whispers fast.
*if (pc_sw_stood_up_day)
