  [b]◈ BLOOD ON THE LANE[/b]
  *line_break
  The last groan dies out between the drystone walls. One shuttered lantern lies cracked on the packed dirt, throwing a low yellow wash across two motionless estate men and the dead hound beside the well.

  Up and down the dark slope, wooden shutters pull quietly shut. Nobody steps onto a doorstep to ask who won.

  The young woman steps out from behind the well, staring wide-eyed at the bodies on the dirt before forcing her breathing steady. "We cannot stay on this lane," she whispers fast. "Nor at the inn—Odda will not risk blood on her stairs with two of the bailiff's men dead outside. There's an empty stone drying shed below the lower terrace wall. Come!"
  *page_break Slip down to the drying shed…
  *set pc_sw_shelter "shed"
  *goto pc_sw_shelter_scene
*else
  *set pc_sw_stage 5
  *set pc_sw_finished true
  *set pc_sw_ending "fled_lane"
  *set minutes_to_pass 10
  *set time_advance_call_id "pc_sw_lane_flee"
  *gosub pc_sw_advance_time
  [b]◈ INTO THE DARK TREES[/b]
  *line_break
  You break clear of the swinging lanterns and vault a low drystone wall into the dense olive rows. Behind you by the well, the woman lets out one sharp cry as heavy hands catch her coat and drag her back up the lane toward the hill. By the time the shouting fades, the bend stands empty.
  *page_break Return to Palmcote's lane…
  *goto pc_sw_exit_lane

