You close your fingers around her arm before she can duck away and raise your voice toward the bobbing lights. "Down here by the well!"

She wrenches hard against your grip, her eyes going wide and cold. "May the hill swallow you," she spits as the two estate hands sprint up, twist her wrists behind her back, and tear the oilcloth bundle out of her hands.

"Bailiff Kelm's up at the pressing house," the nearer man grunts, giving you a sideways nod. "Walk up and collect a finder's fee for saving us a wet chase."

Up at the stone pressing house below the manor wall, a thickset man in a dark coat inspects the wooden box inside the oilcloth with a relieved snort before counting three silver marks into your palm. "House Ferrand remembers useful hands," Bailiff Kelm says flatly, waving his men to shove the girl back toward the loft stairs.

